<p>U.S. forces fired on and disabled two Iranian-flagged oil tankers on Friday in the Gulf of Oman near the Strait of Hormuz, saying the vessels were trying to violate a U.S. blockade of Iranian ports. U.S. Central Command said the tankers were empty, and the Pentagon released video of the strikes. Iran accused Washington of violating an April ceasefire by targeting Iranian ships and striking coastal areas, including Qeshm Island, Bandar Khamir and Sirik. Iranian officials said Tehran responded by attacking U.S. military vessels east of the waterway and south of Chabahar. President Trump said the ceasefire remained in effect while Washington awaited Tehran&#x27;s response to a U.S. proposal to end the war, and Secretary of State Marco Rubio said the United States expected to hear from Iran on Friday.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/bga_S4AExFZ_FcgYQlJQ4tQ4a_CiRWxCSEUX-w_SGPhv1PbQQItsEgr4QVzdsJjGcapDR3lW_HRy4pjxdlQdRBm6PaWuKqmJHShU6YX23K3I' alt='The Arleigh Burke-class guided-missile destroyer USS Rafael Peralta implements a maritime blockade against the Iran-flagged crude oil tanker vessel Herby as it was attempting to sail toward an Iranian port.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Named vessels: Stars and Stripes reported that CENTCOM identified the struck tankers as the M/T Sea Star III and M/T Sevda, both transiting the Gulf of Oman.</li><li>Damage claims: CENTCOM said no U.S. assets were hit after Iranian forces launched missiles, drones and small boats at three Navy destroyers.</li><li>Mission pause: The Guardian reported that the flare-up followed Trump&#x27;s announcement, and then rapid pause, of a new naval mission aimed at opening the strategic waterway.</li><li>Clashes status: Iranian state-affiliated media said later Friday that clashes with U.S. vessels had ceased, though U.S. confirmation was not immediately clear.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>U.S. Central Command: CENTCOM said it did not seek escalation but remained positioned and ready to protect American forces. (<a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/05/07/us-iran-trade-fire-amid-ceasefire-00911016'>Politico</a>)</li><li>Iran&#x27;s UN envoy Amir Saeed Iravani: Iravani told the UN secretary-general and Security Council that the U.S. actions were a breach of Article 2, Paragraph 4 of the UN Charter. (<a href='https://iranpress.com/content/317670'>Iran Press</a>)</li><li>Secretary of State Marco Rubio: Rubio described U.S. strikes on Iranian military facilities as defensive actions. (<a href='https://www.jpost.com/middle-east/iran-news/article-895576'>The Jerusalem Post</a>)</li><li>Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi: Araghchi criticized what he called American military adventures when a diplomatic solution was on the table and said Iran would not yield to pressure. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1998865/us-awaits-iran-reply-even-as-navies-clash-in-hormuz'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/5/8/pentagon-releases-video-of-strikes-on-iranian-oil-tankers'>Pentagon releases video of strikes on Iranian oil tankers</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/90225b9c-707c-4877-931d-5022d1ed583f'>Middle East crisis day 70 as it happened: US strikes 2 Iranian-flagged oil tankers as ceasefire comes under new strains</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/us-fire-on-iran-tankers-sparks-reprisals-as-deal-hangs-in-balance'>US fire on Iran tankers sparks reprisals as deal hangs in balance</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/u-s-strikes-on-iranian-tankers-raise-more-questions-over-negotiations-to-end-war'>U.S. strikes on Iranian tankers raise more questions over negotiations to end war</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/may/08/us-iran-war-strait-of-hormuz-negotiations-marco-rubio'>US awaiting response from Iran over proposals for ceasefire deal, says